  "description": "MOSMAK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H70 Cl2 N8 O14 Yb4 4+,2(Cl4 Zn1 2-),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 5 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 5 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.695-3.824 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.05-114.62°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [C64H70Cl2N8O14Yb4]4+·2[ZnCl4]2−·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Explicit bracketed charge: 4+.",
